13
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:58,700
Alright, so today's question is from our patron from Patreon. Obviously, he has a little preference.

14
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:04,700
So, his subject is artist is a waste of money. Pakistani mentality even in Australia.

15
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:07,340
Hi Mr. Junaid, I hope this email finds you in good health.

16
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:10,987
I come from Pakistan and have been residing in Melbourne for the past 14 years.

17
00:01:11,067 --> 00:01:13,009
I'm a building automation engineer, married,

18
00:01:13,089 --> 00:01:15,340
have two beautiful daughters and life is good here.

19
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:17,009
We enjoy laid back Aussie lifestyle.

20
00:01:17,089 --> 00:01:21,780
I'm also a guitar player slash musician and have been keeping things quiet for the last 10 years.

21
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:29,543
for the past 20 years, basically limiting my hobby to my bedroom.

22
00:01:29,623 --> 00:01:31,208
However, during COVID lockdown,

23
00:01:31,288 --> 00:01:35,918
I got a chance to get in touch with the other Pakistani slash Indian musicians over here.

24
00:01:35,998 --> 00:01:42,140
I started performing at different cultural events in Melbourne when the COVID restrictions started to ease last year.

25
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:47,860
Zahir hai, log khas war pe Australia mein chuki, sabse sakht lockdown da, poori duniya ka.

26
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:52,420
Aur bahut sabse end mein khatam hua, vaccination bhi sabse end mein wahan hui.

27
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,020
I'm sure and I know a lot of people personally who were who were really really losing it because

28
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,810
There was a lot of chaos at home. So I'm sure guitar must have helped you.

29
00:02:00,890 --> 00:02:02,839
help you, you know, to overcome that.

30
00:02:02,919 --> 00:02:08,741
I had been out of touch from our Pakistani community in Australia for the past 12 years and life was so good.

31
00:02:08,821 --> 00:02:10,850
Don't get me wrong, we have a decent.

32
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:16,637
sized like-minded Pakistani friends and family circle who have successfully avoided Pakistani norms,

33
00:02:16,717 --> 00:02:19,740
example, hardcore political discussions back in the 1980s.

34
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:20,806
backbiting, etc.

35
00:02:20,886 --> 00:02:25,673
There are also some positive attributes, for example, punctuality and commitment.

36
00:02:25,753 --> 00:02:26,323
That's good.

37
00:02:26,403 --> 00:02:26,756
However,

38
00:02:26,836 --> 00:02:34,583
performing in the Pakistani events for the past two years has introduced me to the other side of the Pakistani community in Melbourne.

39
00:02:34,663 --> 00:02:38,830
They have the same issues which are quite common in Pakistan, for example,

40
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:42,371
lack of commitment, being always late and many, many more.

41
00:02:42,451 --> 00:02:43,617
For the past two years,

42
00:02:43,697 --> 00:02:47,810
past two years have been the most stressful days in my life in Australia.

43
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,840
Isn't that interesting? Anyways, the focal point of this email is something else.

44
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:58,240
Every time we perform for the Indian audience, we always get paid on time and receive a lot of respect.

45
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:04,960
On the flip side, every time there's a Pakistani event, their first priority is to make us perform for free.

46
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:07,760
They try to use nationalism and etc.

47
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,640
Haan ji, mulk ke liye kaam kar le. You know.

48
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:16,280
Rone shuru ho jate hain, bhai. Kharche ginwana shuru kar dete hain. Hall ka kharcha, catering, etc.

49
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:24,240
Luckily money is not an issue as my income as an engineer is sufficient to support my family in order to enjoy a nice lifestyle.

50
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:31,459
However, as you know, a lot of effort goes into rehearsals and etc for the band.

51
00:03:31,539 --> 00:03:33,960
The gear costs money as well.

52
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:38,360
However, we only charge minimal amounts for these Pakistani events.

53
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:41,480
I will give you an example of my most recent experience.

54
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:53,145
to perform in an event by a Pakistani doctor who is aspiring to be a politician in Australia and trying to seek a ticket in the state elections.

55
00:03:53,225 --> 00:03:58,843
This guy is quite rich and owns chains of clinics and owns clinics, et cetera.

56
00:03:58,923 --> 00:04:04,223
After one week of the event, I asked my band members to chase him for the payment.

57
00:04:04,303 --> 00:04:07,562
However, the first thing that this doctor asked was,

58
00:04:07,642 --> 00:04:10,023
do others pay us for our performances?

59
00:04:10,103 --> 00:04:10,410
I mean, in

60
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:15,710
I mean, instead of just paying the agreed amount, he was trying to analyze whether he should pay or not.

61
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:19,570
We told him, yes, we do get paid for our performances.

62
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:23,070
He then asked for the account details so that he could pay.

63
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:29,000
No amount was received even after two weeks, so I again asked my band member to chase him up.

64
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:30,856
Nothing happened for six weeks,

65
00:04:30,936 --> 00:04:36,230
so I decided to engage myself and wrote a very firm message and pressed really hard on him.

66
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,290
This time he decided to.

67
00:04:37,370 --> 00:04:41,021
to pay as he could see potential for his reputation being damaged.

68
00:04:41,101 --> 00:04:44,294
He paid the exact amount, however, the comment he made was,

69
00:04:44,374 --> 00:04:47,079
I'm not going to run away for X amount of dollars.

70
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:48,999
He could have said that he forgot.

71
00:04:49,079 --> 00:04:52,109
Instead, he made a very sarcastic comment like, come on,

72
00:04:52,189 --> 00:04:55,137
at least you could do is apologize and make it right.

73
00:04:55,217 --> 00:04:57,760
Maybe this is a very common Pakistani behavior.

74
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,842
However, in a country like Australia,

75
00:04:59,922 --> 00:05:04,020
I had all the right to file a report against him at a local police station.

76
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:04,400
Anyways,

77
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:10,880
this was just an example and my band members are now seriously considering not to work with any Pakistani organizers in the future.

78
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:14,708
As I said, we never had any issues with the Indian organizers.

79
00:05:14,788 --> 00:05:17,945
I would love to hear your thoughts on this one.

80
00:05:18,025 --> 00:05:18,917
Am I overreacting?

81
00:05:18,997 --> 00:05:21,345
Should I give leverage to guys like these?

82
00:05:21,425 --> 00:05:24,421
What if my finances were totally dependent upon music?

83
00:05:24,501 --> 00:05:27,362
I would have had to suck up a lot to guys like these.

84
00:05:27,442 --> 00:05:28,792
Sorry for the long email.

85
00:05:28,872 --> 00:05:29,548
Your thoughts.

86
00:05:29,628 --> 00:05:31,670
Thank you so much for your email.

87
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:36,670
This is a very good question because this is something that I go through a lot.

88
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:42,131
The comparison you made between Indian organizers and Pakistani organizers,

89
00:05:42,211 --> 00:05:48,670
you said that Indian organizers always pay on time and the audience always pays respect.

90
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:52,757
This thing, whatever I have done podcasts with musicians,

91
00:05:52,837 --> 00:05:57,750
whether it is Ali Azmat or Gauhar Wali, it has not been released yet.

92
00:05:58,250 --> 00:06:01,570
All the musicians. Everybody said the same thing.

93
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:06,570
In fact, I won't name many of our artists,

94
00:06:06,650 --> 00:06:09,770
their overseas managers, they were always Indian.

95
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:11,202
For the same reason,

96
00:06:11,282 --> 00:06:17,370
because they're very committed and they are very punctual and they're very professional.

97
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:22,770
So, there are many names, I won't name them. But that is the reason.

98
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:25,070
And, in our country, you see.

99
00:06:25,150 --> 00:06:27,750
First of all, we don't value art.

100
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:31,676
I don't understand why our people leave Pakistan for 20 years,

101
00:06:31,756 --> 00:06:34,773
and those countries that are on time,

102
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:39,670
they can't learn a basic thing like coming on time or starting things on time.

103
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:41,070
That's so unfortunate.

104
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:45,190
I think people have killed someone else's right to have a passport.

105
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:51,920
Because if you don't bring these basic things into your life, you can understand that if you start going on time.

106
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:58,920
For example, I had worked on a film. There are two or three films, so I won't tell you which one.

107
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,920
Whatever call time they used to give me, I used to tell them not to worry, it's a cassette.

108
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,920
Okay? Zahid Ahmed and Sabah Qamarwali. So I had four scenes in it.

109
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:12,920
The call time they used to give me, I used to be there at that time. Because you know me, I show the watch in stories.

110
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:18,690
So whenever I went on time, I was always made to sit for six hours. Not now.

111
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:27,690
So the norm here is that an artist never comes on time and it is respected that he is a great artist and never comes on time.

112
00:07:27,770 --> 00:07:29,447
So this is the situation.

113
00:07:29,527 --> 00:07:30,869
So I always traveled.

114
00:07:30,949 --> 00:07:36,013
So I understand that similarly if you reach on time for a wedding in Pakistan,

115
00:07:36,093 --> 00:07:40,470
where it is written 8 PM, then you alone are looking like a chair.

116
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:45,880
I went to an award ceremony, again I will not tell where. The time they gave me, I reached on time.

117
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:52,880
I was standing there and the person who was supposed to sit on the red carpet was rolling out of the car.

118
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,880
So I went and sat in the car and I said, this is the situation.

119
00:07:55,960 --> 00:08:02,880
So in Pakistan, if you follow time, you will be the fool. I'm not saying that you shouldn't.

120
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:07,880
The person should be committed to it, but the biggest loss will be yours.

121
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:13,490
So this is it. But in a country like Australia or America or England, where you know that everything is there from time to time.

122
00:08:13,570 --> 00:08:17,070
So at least learn one thing if you've been there for 20 years.

123
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:19,170
The second thing is that you said,

124
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:22,450
professionalism is very lacking in our country.

125
00:08:22,530 --> 00:08:25,210
These things are not taught in our country, sadly speaking.

126
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:28,190
Although Sikhism is a Muslim language, but if you deal with any business,

127
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:33,510
or any of these events, it is always high and low.

128
00:08:33,710 --> 00:08:36,110
Okay, the thing you said, come for free.

129
00:08:36,190 --> 00:08:38,230
I have heard a lot of these free words.

130
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:44,210
People don't realize this is all I do. This is my livelihood.

131
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:48,050
And not just mine, but of 22 people. Because now we have a team of 22 people.

132
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:53,070
Right? So, many people say, make a video for this and that.

133
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:57,170
Okay, okay. What is your budget? No, do it like this. You have to speak.

134
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:01,570
So I say, if speaking is just a skill, then you speak.

135
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:06,850
Because the line you have written and you have to give me to speak, which you want for free, then you speak.

136
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:16,290
The difference is that I have worked hard for 10-12 years to make the weight of what I'm saying.

137
00:09:16,370 --> 00:09:19,410
Right? So that's a cost. Time is money.

138
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:26,010
So I have put in that time. You must have heard the story that a factory had a problem and a guy called.

139
00:09:26,090 --> 00:09:29,697
Many engineers came, the machine was not working, production was stopped.

140
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,854
Then a completely illiterate mechanic came.

141
00:09:31,934 --> 00:09:35,090
He saw the machine and hit the hammer and the machine started.

142
00:09:35,690 --> 00:09:36,610
He said, $3,000.

143
00:09:36,690 --> 00:09:38,610
I said, you only hit one hammer.

144
00:09:38,690 --> 00:09:40,610
He said, it was $1 to hit the hammer.

145
00:09:40,690 --> 00:09:44,610
Where and how hard you have to hit, it's $2,999.

146
00:09:44,690 --> 00:09:46,610
Because I wasted so many years in this.

147
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:49,610
I didn't waste it, I learned what to do.

148
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:52,610
So people used to say to me very easily that you just have to speak.

149
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:54,610
So I say, then do one thing, you have to speak.

150
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:59,610
Because if you are not appreciating someone's time, then you should not work with such a person. Right?

151
00:09:59,690 --> 00:10:02,690
And to this day, this happens to me today.

152
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:04,421
So, this is one thing.

153
00:10:04,501 --> 00:10:09,525
The second thing is that, for example, in events, for example, I am often called.

154
00:10:09,605 --> 00:10:11,647
Now I don't go to a lot of events.

155
00:10:11,727 --> 00:10:13,708
The main reason for that is this.

156
00:10:13,788 --> 00:10:18,582
Lack of commitment, not starting on time, time is wasted, mismanagement,

157
00:10:18,662 --> 00:10:20,203
crowd control is not there.

158
00:10:20,283 --> 00:10:23,305
And if you ask for compensation for yourself,

159
00:10:23,385 --> 00:10:26,627
they also say that you only need it for an hour.

160
00:10:26,707 --> 00:10:30,070
What you don't realize is that for an hour, I am called.

161
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:32,870
I have to get ready, get in the car, get out of the car.

162
00:10:32,950 --> 00:10:34,270
That takes 4-5 hours.

163
00:10:34,350 --> 00:10:40,070
And in Karachi, if you are 45 minutes away, your whole day's energy is gone.

164
00:10:40,150 --> 00:10:42,070
At least it's mine.

165
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:46,070
Anyway, and often these students do this.

166
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:49,570
And they say that we do not have a budget.

167
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,070
So you come.

168
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:56,150
So I say, brother, you have organized some events like this.

169
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:58,860
Some students wanted to attend the event.

170
00:10:58,940 --> 00:11:02,860
I was the only person there.

171
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:05,860
So because of me, that event was happening.

172
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:10,860
Now, in that event, there was a kid who said, there is no budget, you can come for free.

173
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:13,444
I said, in that event, you have made a stage,

174
00:11:13,524 --> 00:11:17,500
you told the stage person that there is no budget, you gave him money,

175
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:21,776
you also gave the sound person, you also gave the light person,

176
00:11:21,856 --> 00:11:23,940
you also gave the decoration person.

177
00:11:24,230 --> 00:11:31,912
You gave chairs, you gave photographers, you gave caterers,

178
00:11:31,993 --> 00:11:35,950
you are giving money to everyone.

179
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:40,606
But the person who is creating the event, you are not giving it to him.

180
00:11:40,686 --> 00:11:42,223
How is that even sensible?

181
00:11:42,303 --> 00:11:44,950
Do you understand what I am saying?

182
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:51,030
But they are children and our university does not understand this thing.

183
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:54,910
So I have to apologize. Most of the times.

184
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:57,530
So this is absolutely right.

185
00:11:57,610 --> 00:12:00,870
See, my learning is to take money first.

186
00:12:01,170 --> 00:12:07,050
Take money first, but there are some clients who have a cycle that we give after 3 months.

187
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:08,710
There are big clients.

188
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:14,050
There is a very big bank. It has not given money to many YouTubers since January.

189
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:17,390
Okay? And every time they say.

190
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:20,390
On Friday, you will get a check. Listen to this carefully.

191
00:12:20,470 --> 00:12:26,390
All the people listening, if someone tells you that on Friday you will get a check, on Friday you will get a payment, that will never happen.

192
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,200
Because on Friday, the cap is very good.

193
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:31,950
You will chase in the morning and say that after Friday prayer, then lunch is done,

194
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:35,390
then they come at 3.30 and sit at the desk, at 5 o'clock office is closed.

195
00:12:35,470 --> 00:12:39,390
On Friday, there is never a payment. You can take this from me.

196
00:12:39,470 --> 00:12:41,390
Mashallah, it is a blessed day, everyone goes to prayer.

197
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:44,470
The same day's name is used to lie.

198
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:49,020
So he kept on doing it and January's payment came today, November.

199
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:55,020
I stop every day because the problem is that I just put up stories that they didn't give me money.

200
00:12:55,100 --> 00:13:00,020
The agency through which it came, if tomorrow the bank stops working with that agency,

201
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:05,020
boys and girls work in that agency, their job will not go, their one big client will go.

202
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:09,020
Their jobs can suffer because of my one story. Right?

203
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:12,100
So now this is a big situation and they know this.

204
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:15,470
or this or that, or whatever.

205
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,110
Problems are problems.

206
00:13:17,490 --> 00:13:21,630
So in most cases, like big brands, they give.

207
00:13:21,710 --> 00:13:24,750
I mean, what will Coca-Cola do with my 5 lakh rupees?

208
00:13:24,830 --> 00:13:27,170
Such a big company, I'm giving an example, right?

209
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:31,910
But if there are companies, then you should buy from them before.

210
00:13:31,990 --> 00:13:33,910
Before performance, before going on stage.

211
00:13:33,990 --> 00:13:35,910
Say, I will not show until my payment is done.

212
00:13:35,990 --> 00:13:37,510
He will do it from anywhere and give it to you.

213
00:13:37,590 --> 00:13:39,590
And you tell this before.

214
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,800
Otherwise, you keep chasing.

215
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:47,400
And there have been many cases where you keep chasing and that's it.

216
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:52,264
And the main reason is that you talked about how the Indian audience gives a lot of respect,

217
00:13:52,344 --> 00:13:54,900
but you only do Pakistani shows, so that's not it.

218
00:13:54,980 --> 00:14:00,700
In our country, generally, artists are not supported and not given respect.

219
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:05,320
We call musicians very easily, but without Spotify, we are not.

220
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:12,120
Neither our car travels, nor our Kareem Uber travels, nor we listen to Spotify before going to sleep at night.

221
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:13,120
Do you understand what I'm saying?

222
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:17,606
We have to spend without Netflix, we have to spend without YouTube,

223
00:14:17,686 --> 00:14:22,393
we have to watch videos, we have to watch vlogs, we have to follow influencers,

224
00:14:22,473 --> 00:14:23,970
but they are still barren.

225
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:29,720
So generally, like in masses, I'm not saying that all, obviously a lot of people love us as well.

